Usage:

```tsx
<AccountSettingsScreen
  user={{ name: 'Jordan Lee', email: 'jordan@example.com' }}
  onEditProfile={() => navigation.navigate('EditProfile')}
  onNavigate={(key) => navigation.navigate(key)}
  onToggleChange={(key, value) => api.updatePreference(key, value)}
  onDeleteAccount={() => api.deleteAccount()}
  onDeleted={() => signOut()}
/>
```

Notes:
- Requires `react-native-safe-area-context` (standard in most RN apps for notch/inset handling); swap in `SafeAreaView` from `react-native` if you don't have it.
- Deletion requires typing `DELETE` before the button enables, with inline error display and a spinner during the async call — the modal can't be dismissed mid-request.
- Toggle rows manage local state but report changes via `onToggleChange` so you can persist them; pass `initialToggles` to hydrate from server state.
- Styling uses platform-aware shadows (`shadowColor`/`shadowOpacity` on iOS, `elevation` on Android) and works in both light-mode contexts without extra tuning.
